00:46:59.280 --> 00:47:05.280
And he has met you. He has met you in that place.

00:47:05.280 --> 00:47:08.280
In the midst of your loss, in your grief.

00:47:08.280 --> 00:47:11.280
But he does not stop there.

00:47:11.280 --> 00:47:16.280
He is, according to 1 Peter 3.18, doing what?

00:47:16.280 --> 00:47:19.280
Bringing you to God.

00:47:19.280 --> 00:47:22.280
That's a word for someone here tonight.

00:47:22.280 --> 00:47:26.280
He is bringing you to God.

00:47:26.280 --> 00:47:32.280
Bringing you, each and every one of you, to God.

00:47:32.280 --> 00:47:36.280
Christ is offering you a hand.

00:47:36.280 --> 00:47:41.280
Not only of empathy, though it is that.

00:47:41.280 --> 00:47:44.280
Not only of presence.

00:47:44.280 --> 00:47:51.280
Christ being with you in the midst of the hell you have gone through or are currently going through.

00:47:51.280 --> 00:47:54.280
Because Lord knows, some of us are going through it right now.

00:47:55.280 --> 00:47:59.280
But it's not only empathy, though it is that.

00:47:59.280 --> 00:48:02.280
It's more than that, though.

00:48:02.280 --> 00:48:06.280
He is offering you a power.

00:48:06.280 --> 00:48:13.280
And by his Holy Spirit, he is bringing you out of that pit.

00:48:13.280 --> 00:48:16.280
Friends, I could have you speak, no matter what you're going through,

00:48:16.280 --> 00:48:19.280
I could have you speak to half a dozen people tonight

00:48:19.280 --> 00:48:25.280
who have been there in that thing and Christ has brought them out.

00:48:28.280 --> 00:48:35.280
Christ loves you with a furious and a passionate love.

00:48:35.280 --> 00:48:39.280
Christ is fighting for you.

00:48:41.280 --> 00:48:43.280
Have you been there?

00:48:43.280 --> 00:48:46.280
In hell?

00:48:47.280 --> 00:48:50.280
As a perpetrator?

00:48:50.280 --> 00:48:53.280
This one's harder.

00:48:53.280 --> 00:48:59.280
Have you felt there's no forgiveness of sins for you?

00:49:06.280 --> 00:49:13.280
Because what you did, it wasn't like just wrong, the mistake.

00:49:13.280 --> 00:49:16.280
It wasn't just wrong that could easily be set right.

00:49:16.280 --> 00:49:19.280
It was something else.

00:49:19.280 --> 00:49:24.280
It was sin.

00:49:24.280 --> 00:49:26.280
It was evil. It was hurtful.

00:49:26.280 --> 00:49:32.280
Have you felt in your bones that if people knew what you had done, they would reject you?

00:49:32.280 --> 00:49:35.280
And that's why you just keep it, just buried.

00:49:35.280 --> 00:49:37.280
Just buried.

00:49:37.280 --> 00:49:40.280
Maybe even go to a meetup or small group where you're like,

00:49:40.280 --> 00:49:43.280
we're not going there.

00:49:43.280 --> 00:49:46.280
We're just not going there.

00:49:50.280 --> 00:49:53.280
Have you been there in that hell?

00:49:53.280 --> 00:49:56.280
Are you there now?

00:49:56.280 --> 00:50:00.280
The gospel of Jesus Christ sounds in your ears.

00:50:00.280 --> 00:50:02.280
Verse 18,

00:50:02.280 --> 00:50:06.280
Christ also suffered once for sins,

00:50:06.280 --> 00:50:09.280
the righteous for the unrighteous,

00:50:09.280 --> 00:50:13.280
to bring you to God.

00:50:13.280 --> 00:50:16.280
Yes, you were, pick your metaphor,

00:50:16.280 --> 00:50:21.280
unrighteous, unclean, prone to every form of evil,

00:50:21.280 --> 00:50:26.280
but Christ, the righteous one, the innocent one, has died on your behalf.

00:50:26.280 --> 00:50:30.280
He's gone to the depths of the hell that you've made.

00:50:30.280 --> 00:50:34.280
The depths of the hell perhaps that you even plunged others into.

00:50:34.280 --> 00:50:41.280
But he now offers you forgiveness of sins and a new life.

00:50:41.280 --> 00:50:49.280
See, Christ has harrowed, has fought, has overcome hell.

00:50:49.280 --> 00:50:54.280
Christ has gone down into the depths of your sheol.

00:50:54.280 --> 00:50:59.280
Christ too has been abused and violated and ashamed.

00:50:59.280 --> 00:51:03.280
Christ went all the way down into death,

00:51:03.280 --> 00:51:06.280
but he did not stay there.

00:51:06.280 --> 00:51:11.280
There is a greater power than the power of the devil.

00:51:11.280 --> 00:51:15.280
There is a greater power than the power of hell.

00:51:15.280 --> 00:51:20.280
There is a greater power than the power of your depression

00:51:20.280 --> 00:51:24.280
or your abuse or your rejection

00:51:24.280 --> 00:51:32.280
by people you loved, church leaders, pastors, friends, family.

00:51:34.280 --> 00:51:37.280
There is a greater power than that.

00:51:37.280 --> 00:51:43.280
Christ is the greater power and he is now trampling hell

00:51:43.280 --> 00:51:48.280
and he is leading you and all people out.

00:51:48.280 --> 00:51:52.280
You see, since Christ descended into hell,

00:51:52.280 --> 00:51:58.280
that means no one is beyond his reach.

00:52:00.280 --> 00:52:03.280
No one is beyond his reach.

00:52:03.280 --> 00:52:07.280
You are not beyond his reach.

00:52:10.280 --> 00:52:15.280
I've often wondered about Judas Iscariot.

00:52:15.280 --> 00:52:19.280
He, of course, the infamous disciple

00:52:19.280 --> 00:52:24.280
who betrayed Jesus for 30 pieces of silver.

00:52:24.280 --> 00:52:27.280
I've wondered what went through his mind.

00:52:27.280 --> 00:52:33.280
There's even the details of the story and how it all happened.

00:52:33.280 --> 00:52:37.280
You remember he was going to lead a mob of soldiers to Christ

00:52:37.280 --> 00:52:40.280
and they didn't exactly know which of the 12,

00:52:40.280 --> 00:52:44.280
or I guess 13, well, 12 because Judas isn't in the group,

00:52:44.280 --> 00:52:46.280
which ones Christ.

00:52:46.280 --> 00:52:50.280
You remember how he was going to single Jesus out,

00:52:50.280 --> 00:52:52.280
the one that they should arrest.

00:52:52.280 --> 00:52:54.280
You remember what it was?

00:52:54.280 --> 00:52:56.280
Kiss on the cheek.

00:52:56.280 --> 00:53:02.280
Like in that culture, this kind of picture of friendship and connection.

00:53:03.280 --> 00:53:05.280
And he does it.

00:53:05.280 --> 00:53:07.280
Walks right up.

00:53:11.280 --> 00:53:14.280
For 30 pieces of silver.

00:53:14.280 --> 00:53:17.280
Christ, of course, is arrested, condemned to die,

00:53:17.280 --> 00:53:20.280
and then it all hits Judas at some point.

00:53:20.280 --> 00:53:22.280
It all hits him.

00:53:22.280 --> 00:53:24.280
And he is undone.

00:53:24.280 --> 00:53:27.280
You remember he goes back to the religious leaders.

00:53:27.280 --> 00:53:28.280
You remember what he does?

00:53:28.280 --> 00:53:30.280
He tries to give back the money.

00:53:30.280 --> 00:53:33.280
It's a lot of money in that culture.

00:53:33.280 --> 00:53:34.280
Tries to give it back.

00:53:34.280 --> 00:53:36.280
You can see in that moment, what's he doing?

00:53:36.280 --> 00:53:39.280
He's trying to distance himself from what he's done.

00:53:39.280 --> 00:53:42.280
Like trying to make right what he cannot make right.

00:53:42.280 --> 00:53:44.280
But he's trying.

00:53:44.280 --> 00:53:45.280
I've been there.

00:53:45.280 --> 00:53:46.280
Trying.

00:53:46.280 --> 00:53:48.280
It won't work, but you try.

00:53:48.280 --> 00:53:53.280
And he actually tells them, he says,

00:53:53.280 --> 00:53:55.280
I've betrayed innocent blood.

00:53:55.280 --> 00:53:57.280
That's his statement.

00:53:57.280 --> 00:53:59.280
I've betrayed innocent blood.

00:54:03.280 --> 00:54:06.280
And then soon after that, he, of course, despairs.

00:54:07.280 --> 00:54:08.280
Right?

00:54:08.280 --> 00:54:12.280
No forgiveness of sins for him, his mind.

00:54:12.280 --> 00:54:16.280
And so, of course, he ends up committing suicide that night.

00:54:19.280 --> 00:54:21.280
So sometimes I like to imagine, though,

00:54:21.280 --> 00:54:24.280
what if Judas did not despair?

00:54:24.280 --> 00:54:28.280
What if he did not count himself among those

00:54:28.280 --> 00:54:31.280
who could not be forgiven?

00:54:31.280 --> 00:54:36.280
What if he didn't see himself as someone so far gone

00:54:36.280 --> 00:54:40.280
that the love of God could not find him?

00:54:40.280 --> 00:54:43.280
I like to imagine what the resurrected Jesus

00:54:43.280 --> 00:54:46.280
might have said to him.

00:54:46.280 --> 00:54:49.280
Like maybe a word of forgiveness.

00:54:49.280 --> 00:54:51.280
Maybe a word of healing.

00:54:54.280 --> 00:54:57.280
Or maybe he did.

00:54:57.280 --> 00:55:02.280
Maybe down there in those shadowy depths of Sheol,

00:55:02.280 --> 00:55:05.280
maybe Christ did speak to Judas.

00:55:07.280 --> 00:55:11.280
Maybe he did forgive.

00:55:11.280 --> 00:55:16.280
Maybe even brought him out, just like Christ does,

00:55:16.280 --> 00:55:20.280
each and every single one of us.

00:55:20.280 --> 00:55:23.280
In the name of the Father, the Son, and the Holy Spirit.

00:55:23.280 --> 00:55:25.280
Amen.

00:55:26.280 --> 00:55:30.280
So as we come to the table of the Lord tonight,

00:55:30.280 --> 00:55:33.280
I know that was really intense.

00:55:33.280 --> 00:55:36.280
It's Lent.

00:55:36.280 --> 00:55:40.280
As we come to the table of the Lord tonight,

00:55:40.280 --> 00:55:46.280
we do it as the people being brought out.

00:55:46.280 --> 00:55:49.280
As we take in the body of Christ in the bread,

00:55:49.280 --> 00:55:52.280
the blood of Christ in the wine,

00:55:52.280 --> 00:55:55.280
it's this moment of connection,

00:55:55.280 --> 00:55:59.280
it's this moment of presence,

00:55:59.280 --> 00:56:01.280
where Christ is present to us

00:56:01.280 --> 00:56:06.280
in the midst of whatever hell you might be going through.

00:56:06.280 --> 00:56:09.280
And I pray, just like Mindy prayed earlier,

00:56:09.280 --> 00:56:16.280
I pray it's a moment of a little bit of joy

00:56:16.280 --> 00:56:19.280
in the midst of whatever you find yourself

00:56:19.280 --> 00:56:21.280
going through in this season.

00:56:21.280 --> 00:56:24.280
So the way we'll do this

00:56:24.280 --> 00:56:27.280
is we'll just kind of form a line right here,

00:56:27.280 --> 00:56:29.280
and we'll start kind of at the front rows

00:56:29.280 --> 00:56:30.280
and just work our way back.

00:56:30.280 --> 00:56:32.280
We don't do, like, ushers or anything.

00:56:32.280 --> 00:56:34.280
You just kind of just feel it out, you know?

00:56:34.280 --> 00:56:40.280
And the red is wine, and the white is grape juice,

00:56:40.280 --> 00:56:43.280
for those who care about such things.

00:56:43.280 --> 00:56:48.280
And we practice what's called an open table,

00:56:48.280 --> 00:56:50.280
meaning if you're here tonight

00:56:50.280 --> 00:56:52.280
and you want to participate,

00:56:52.280 --> 00:56:55.280
then you are free to do that.

00:56:55.280 --> 00:56:56.280
You just come forward,

00:56:56.280 --> 00:56:59.280
regardless of denomination or, you know, whatever,

00:56:59.280 --> 00:57:03.280
or exact theologies, you're free to participate.

00:57:03.280 --> 00:57:05.280
So let me invite you to the table.

00:57:05.280 --> 00:57:07.280
This is a Celtic Christian invitation.

00:57:07.280 --> 00:57:09.280
This is the table,

00:57:09.280 --> 00:57:12.280
not of the church, but of the Lord.

00:57:12.280 --> 00:57:14.280
And it's made ready for those who love him

00:57:14.280 --> 00:57:17.280
and for those who want to love him more.

00:57:17.280 --> 00:57:19.280
So come.

00:57:19.280 --> 00:57:22.280
You who have much faith and you who have little.

00:57:22.280 --> 00:57:24.280
You who have been here often

00:57:24.280 --> 00:57:27.280
and you who have not been here long.

00:57:27.280 --> 00:57:30.280
You who have tried to follow

00:57:30.280 --> 00:57:33.280
and you who have failed.

00:57:33.280 --> 00:57:34.280
Come.

00:57:34.280 --> 00:57:39.280
Come, because it's the Lord Jesus himself who invites you,

00:57:39.280 --> 00:57:41.280
and it's his will that those who want to meet him

00:57:41.280 --> 00:57:44.280
should meet him here.

00:57:44.280 --> 00:57:46.280
Come to the table.

